    "summary": " deployment has been modified since install (all at revision 1, generation 1).\n- **Flags:** Every flagd flag is off. I checked both the ConfigMap and the live flagd evaluation.\n- **Accounting:**\n  - It is consuming the `orders` topic on Kafka. Consumer lag is about 3 messages.\n  - The only error in its logs is a one-time \"Unknown topic or partition: orders\" at startup, before the topic existed.\n  - The database has no blocked or long-running queries, and CPU and memory are normal.\n- **Chatbot and mcp:**\n  - Both have endpoints and are serving. `/chatbot/` returns 200 through frontend-proxy and directly. `/mcp` answers 406, which is expected for a request that isn't MCP.\n  - Neither has logged any incoming requests. The load generator only calls the frontend and the agent.\n  - The agent has `MCP_ENABLED=False`, so nothing sends traffic to mcp. This looks like the baseline configuration, not something broken.\n- **Network policy:** `frontend-ingress` was created after the rest of the namespace, but it allows all ingress, so it isn't blocking anything.\n- **Collector:** The otel-collector can't export to `jaeger-collector.opentelemetry-collectors\u2026:4317` (connection refused), and the agent also logs 503s on span export. This is an observability-pipeline problem, not a request-path one.\n\n**Likely explanation (not confirmed)**\n- The accounting latency alert probably came from the startup race: it began consuming before the Kafka topic existed, and it has since caught up.\n- The NoRequestsReceived alerts for chatbot and mcp fit those services receiving no traffic. They could also fit the collector's failed exports leaving the alert metrics incomplete.\n\nI didn't flip `MCP_ENABLED` or edit the collector config, because I had no evidence either was the cause and both would change the system's behavior.\n\n**Next steps for the team:** Confirm whether the alerts have cleared. If they haven't, look at the Jaeger exporter target and whether chatbot and mcp are expected to get traffic.",
    "timed_out": false,
